---
import FeatureSection from "@/components/FeatureSection.astro";
import FeatureMedia from "@/components/ui/FeatureMedia.astro";
import Lede from "@/components/ui/Lede.astro";
import browserImage from "@/assets/browser.png";
---
<FeatureSection
  id="browser"
  eyebrow="Browser"
  heading="See the app your agent is building."
  index="04"
  reverse
  accent="yellow"
>
  <FeatureMedia
    slot="media"
    src={browserImage}
    alt="CadencR browser pane showing the demo app's settings page with dark mode enabled, next to the agent's browser tool calls that opened, clicked, and verified it"
    reverse
    caption="Actual capture — the agent verifying its own change"
  />
  <Fragment slot="lede">
    <Lede>
      CadencR ships with a <span class="em">real embedded browser</span>. Point a pane at your dev
      server and watch changes land — no window juggling, no lost context.
    </Lede>
    <Lede class="mt-2.5">
      Better: the agent can drive it. It opens the page it just changed, clicks through the flow,
      and reads the console — <span class="em">before</span> telling you it's done.
    </Lede>
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="bullets">
    <li><strong>Live preview</strong> — your dev server in a pane beside the stream.</li>
    <li><strong>Tabs scoped per task</strong> — switch sessions and the tabs follow.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Agent-driven QA</strong> — agents open pages, click, screenshot, and read the
      console over MCP.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Real Chromium</strong> — an actual browser pane, not an iframe preview.</li>
  </Fragment>
</FeatureSection>
